  "body": "Asked for by the maintainer in chat on 2026-11-16:\n\n> Issue; The fixtures page should be able to rotate fixture like the models page can move a model using quarter turns or numerical input to be applied.\n\nWhat is wanted:\n\n- The Fixtures page gets rotation controls for the selected fixture.\n- The controls are the same as those of the Model page: quarter-turn buttons for each axis, and number inputs that the user applies.\n- The layout and the labels follow the Model page, so that the two pages work the same way.\n\nNotes:\n\n- The rotation is an undoable command (AGENTS.md \"Everything Is a Command\"). Undo restores the earlier orientation.\n- The command ships with its MCP tool, or the PR names a follow-up issue `MCP: <command>`.\n- The orientation of a fixture is input to the fixture collision checks and to the carried-workholding check. Those checks must read the rotated shape. The work is thus under the safety floor.\n- A fixture that holds the model or the stock must keep a defined relation to them after the rotation. The PR says which rule it uses, and records it in `docs/decisions/`.\n- Related: #2172 (bodies stand on the floor of the work envelope) and #2173 (locate the stock on a vise) change the same page and placement code. Stack this work on them, or work it after them.\n\nDone means:\n\n- A test pins a quarter turn of a fixture about each axis, and a typed angle, with undo and redo.\n- A test pins that the collision checks read the rotated fixture.\n- The structural UI test asserts the new controls on the Fixtures page (labels, roles, enabled state).\n- The MCP tool exists, or the follow-up issue is named in the PR.\n",
